# Per-workspace isolation overrides.
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. Parallel worktrees get a generated `.env.local`
# (git-ignored) from scripts/agent/setup-worktree.sh with unique free ports.
# Never commit `.env.local`. Never edit the ports by hand — let the script pick them.
#
# Prefer: bash scripts/agent/setup-workspace.sh <slug>
# (solo on idle primary; worktree when primary is busy — see ADR 0004)
#
# The primary checkout can run without any .env.local: docker-compose and
# vite.config.js fall back to the default ports shown below.

# --- Host-published ports (must be unique per worktree) ---
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
REDIS_PORT=6379
API_PORT=8000
FRONTEND_PORT=5173

# --- Compose project name (isolates containers/volumes/networks per worktree) ---
# setup-worktree.sh sets this to the sanitized branch name.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=imoveis

# --- API edge credential (required for SPA favourites / watchlist / admin) ---
# Paste this same value into the sidebar "API credential" field after opening the UI.
# Never commit real production secrets. Restart the stack after changing this.
API_KEY=local-dev-api-key

# --- Host-side cloud backfill runner contract (ADR 0006) ---
# The systemd unit installed by `bash scripts/install-backfill-runner.sh` reads
# THIS file via EnvironmentFile=, so these three are the runner's whole env
# contract. The key lives here and only here — never in a committed file, never
# in a container's environment. Uncomment and fill in with real values.
#
# Cloud key for the Gemma/Gemini backfill (maps to ai.gemini_api_key).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=your-google-ai-studio-key
#
# REQUIRED for a host-side run: the config default database name is NOT the
# primary one. The primary compose stack's DB is `realestate` — without this the
# runner would connect to a database that does not exist.
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://imoveis:<password>@localhost:5432/realestate
#
# Needed whenever REDIS_PORT above is not the default 6379 (the runner talks to
# the primary stack's PUBLISHED port from the host, not from inside the network).
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
#
# --- Cloud enablement: THIS is the switch (story v0.13-s3.5) ---
# `--serve` validates AI routing before its poll loop: it drives ONE cloud client
# and has no local mode, so it needs ALL THREE classes below routed to the SAME
# cloud backend. Set none of them, only some of them, or split them between
# `gemma` and `gemini`, and it exits at startup — the unit then restarts every
# 10 s. `bash scripts/install-backfill-runner.sh --check` reports the effective
# map (YAML + these overrides) and names any class still routed local.
#
# Set them HERE, per host — never in the committed `configs/app_config.yaml`:
# that file must stay all-local (NFR-1) and is pinned there by
# `src/tests/unit/test_config.py::test_enrichment_routing_default_all_local`,
# so editing it turns the merge gate red for every later story. These overrides
# go through the same config loader (`IMOVEIS_<SECTION>__<KEY>`), set the three
# leaves over the YAML map so it stays total, leave the scalar `ai.backend`
# local (the live Celery path is unaffected), and never enter git.
# No `export ` prefix: systemd's EnvironmentFile= is not a shell and would keep
# it literally, leaving the variable unset in the service.
# IMOVEIS_AI__ENRICHMENT_ROUTING__VISUAL=gemma
# IMOVEIS_AI__ENRICHMENT_ROUTING__SENTIMENT=gemma
# IMOVEIS_AI__ENRICHMENT_ROUTING__DEAL_VERDICT=gemma
#
# --- What the local gates read from this file ---
# validate.sh / finish-feature.sh do NOT source this file. They read a fixed,
# default-deny allowlist of workspace-identity keys through
# scripts/agent/lib.sh::load_workspace_env (DW-33):
#   COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME
#   POSTGRES_PORT, POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD, POSTGRES_DB
#   REDIS_PORT, API_PORT, FRONTEND_PORT, PLAYWRIGHT_PORT, PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL
#   POSTGRES_TEST_DB, TEST_DATABASE_URL, REDIS_TEST_DB  (the optional test-DB
#     selectors documented at the BOTTOM of this file)
#   API_KEY, JWT_SECRET
# That is what the loader LOOKS FOR — this template does not assign all of them:
# setup-worktree.sh generates the per-worktree ports and PLAYWRIGHT_PORT,
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD only matters when you override the compose default, and
# validate.sh seeds throwaway API_KEY/JWT_SECRET values when they are unset.
# Everything else here stops at that boundary: the runner contract in this
# section (GEMINI_API_KEY, DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL, every IMOVEIS_* override) and
# any key a future edit adds are never handed to pytest.
# The filter applies to THIS FILE, not to your shell — a variable you exported
# yourself still reaches the gate, so the suite additionally strips the IMOVEIS_*
# override channel in src/tests/conftest.py whatever its origin.

# --- Optional: isolated DB for host pytest (validate.sh defaults to realestate_test) ---
# Scrapers/API Compose keep using POSTGRES_DB=realestate. Do not point TEST_DATABASE_URL
# at the scraped primary database — integration fixtures truncate all tables.
# POSTGRES_TEST_DB=realestate_test
# TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://imoveis:imoveis_local_dev@localhost:5432/realestate_test

# --- Optional: isolated Redis logical DB for host pytest (validate.sh defaults to 15) ---
# Compose API/Celery keep REDIS_URL .../0. Integration flushdb must not hit DB 0.
# REDIS_TEST_DB=15
